+## Deploy on Wasmer
+
+[![Deploy to Wasmer](https://img.shields.io/badge/Deploy%20to-Wasmer-6B4EFF)](https://wasmer.io/apps/create?github=streamlit%2Fllm-examples)
+
+[Wasmer Edge](https://wasmer.io) installs `requirements.txt` and runs the app with Streamlit. The entry file here is `Chatbot.py`, which Wasmer does not pick up by name, so set the start command to `streamlit run Chatbot.py --server.port $PORT --server.address 0.0.0.0 --server.headless true` when creating the app. No secrets are needed to deploy: each page asks for the OpenAI or Anthropic API key in the sidebar and keeps it only for that browser session. The button deploys this repository as-is and does not fork it; to change the examples, fork the repo and connect your fork from the Wasmer dashboard.
